# What gets UPLOADED to Vercel — and therefore what can be served.
#
# vercel.json sets "outputDirectory": ".", so the repository root IS the site:
# every uploaded file is also reachable as a static asset. Production was
# serving api/_identityStore.js, test/**, lib/**, the design/architecture
# markdown and the internal engine directories as raw source because of this.
#
# This list is an ALLOW-LIST, not a deny-list: "/*" excludes every top-level
# entry, and only the entries below are added back. A new document, engine or
# script added to the repository is therefore private by default and cannot be
# published by forgetting to add it here — which is the property a deny-list
# cannot give us.
#
# Note "/*" is anchored to the root, so re-including a directory re-includes
# all of its contents; there is no need to list files inside it.
/*

# --- the app the browser loads -------------------------------------------
!/index.html
!/sw.js
!/manifest.json
!/404.html
!/privacy.html
!/terms.html
!/robots.txt
!/icon.svg
!/brand

# --- ES modules imported at runtime by index.html (and by api/*.js) -------
!/performance
!/season-intelligence
!/src
!/tactics

# --- serverless functions ------------------------------------------------
# Must be uploaded: Vercel builds api/**/*.js into functions. Being uploaded
# also makes the source statically reachable, so vercel.json additionally
# refuses to serve /api/*.js as a file.
!/api

# --- needed by the build, not by the browser -----------------------------
# package.json/package-lock.json install the function dependencies and
# build-inject.js stamps the version into index.html ("build" script).
# Vercel already declines to serve package.json; vercel.json covers the rest.
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/build-inject.js
!/vercel.json

# --- internal files that live inside the re-included directories ---------
# Re-including a directory re-includes everything in it, and these are the
# parts the browser never loads: design documentation, and the Node CLI/API
# entry points for the season engine. Nothing imports them (checked), so
# excluding them costs nothing and keeps the published set to what runs.
performance/README.md
performance/docs/
brand/README.md
season-intelligence/season-api.js
season-intelligence/season-cli.js

# --- work in progress, deliberately not deployed (pre-existing) ----------
# Listed after the re-includes above so these still win.
api/mission-control.js
mission-control/
